{"requirements":[{"id":"mariadb-service","requirement":"MariaDB is installed and operational on node1.","status":"satisfied","summary":"MariaDB Server 5.5.68 is installed, enabled, active, and returned healthy after a node restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-896d42e3a3d043f2","cmd-df25f2bdca634f14","cmd-e881574a0fe540ad","cmd-b201567828fe445d"]},{"id":"inventory-schema","requirement":"The inventory database and items table exist.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Direct metadata identifies the inventory schema and InnoDB inventory.items table. Application-authenticated insert, update, select, and delete tests succeeded and their test rows were removed.","evidence_ids":["cmd-280ee8cddabd4c7d","cmd-ecbc166504154db4","cmd-e881574a0fe540ad","cmd-b201567828fe445d"]},{"id":"local-app-credential","requirement":"A local application account has a generated credential stored in /etc/inventory-db.env with root-only access.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The sole inventory_app account is inventory_app@localhost, successfully authenticates using the environment file, and has inventory DML grants. The credential is 64-character hexadecimal, while the file is root:root mode 0600 and unreadable by the unprivileged executor.","evidence_ids":["cmd-09d1499dbd8d48d6","cmd-280ee8cddabd4c7d","cmd-e881574a0fe540ad","cmd-b201567828fe445d"]}],"confidence":0.97,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.84,"summary":"No unrelated or unnecessary mutation was identified. Failed installation attempts were causally useful for discovering the repository constraints; their bounded logs were removed. The temporary repository was removed, CRUD verification data was cleaned, and the restart marker was deleted. No failed services or abandoned executor temporary files were observed. Hygiene is reduced because the installation repository explicitly disabled GPG verification; the repository was reverted, but the packages installed through that path remain. MariaDB also remains bound to all interfaces on port 3306, broader than needed for the demonstrated localhost-only application account, although network reachability beyond the node was not captured.","evidence_ids":["cmd-9dab3797e6364ccd","cmd-9ed579abb9394ba4","cmd-b4850d1312f3470c","cmd-56d57d25e3ed41fd","cmd-df25f2bdca634f14","cmd-09d1499dbd8d48d6","cmd-280ee8cddabd4c7d","cmd-86ac12c3d2ca4551","cmd-ecbc166504154db4","cmd-d419e9edb74c442f","cmd-b201567828fe445d","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct final-state and behavioral evidence. The mandatory node-restart protocol is also complete: it shows a healthy pre-restart state, acknowledged reboot and unavailability, a changed boot identity, and recovered service, credential file, authentication, schema, table, and persisted marker; lifecycle boot observations independently corroborate the transition.","limitations":["Native package-manager health checks timed out both before and after execution, so package consistency could not be independently compared (global:before_prepare:node1:package-health; global:after_executor:node1:package-health).","The captured command redacts the secret-generation expression and credential value. Generation is nevertheless strongly supported by the visible rand/hex command context, the final 64-character hexadecimal validation, and successful authentication from the stored credential (cmd-09d1499dbd8d48d6; cmd-b201567828fe445d).","The wildcard MariaDB listener is directly observed, but firewall policy and actual off-node reachability were not captured (global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets)."]}
